"id":3941700386,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q8ZMi","user":{"login":"tvenclovas96","id":144885265,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKLGEQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/144885265?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96","html_url":"https://github.com/tvenclovas96","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T21:01:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T21:01:31Z","body":"It would be handy to reference a class member in the tooltip in the way doc string tooltips do, but idk how that could be done","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3941700386/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3944127948","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116623#issuecomment-3944127948","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116623","id":3944127948,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rFp3M","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T11:10:08Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T11:10:08Z","body":"I'm not convinced a singular \"play\" button is a good solution to the problem. If you're playing audio with a button, how do you stop it? \nIf anything, i would expect a small player UI where I can play, pause, and seek the audio. \nBut i think the stream selection already has this, no?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3944127948/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3944815589","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116623#issuecomment-3944815589","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116623","id":3944815589,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rIRvl","user":{"login":"tvenclovas96","id":144885265,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKLGEQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/144885265?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96","html_url":"https://github.com/tvenclovas96","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T13:33:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T14:37:11Z","body":"> I'm not convinced a singular \"play\" button is a good solution to the problem. If you're playing audio with a button, how do you stop it? If anything, i would expect a small player UI where I can play, pause, and seek the audio. But i think the stream selection already has this, no?\r\n\r\nAt least I'm unaware of any existing audio controls to play/seek/stop related to stream players. Even if there is something purely for streams, the 2D and 3D stream players also provide location data to the audio, which does come into play in the editor, so the player nodes still benefit from something.\r\n\r\nSince this just hooks into the existing `.play()` method, `playing` is automatically set to true in the inspector, and you can disable it. Doesn't sound very ergonomic, so at least a `Stop Audio` button sounds reasonable.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if a full-blown ui with seeking makes sense in this specific context - it might make the node inspector too cluttered, and the expected use case for this is geared more towards sound effects, where you might want to try and overlap sounds or play many in quick succession.\r\nAdmittedly, I do miss more advanced controls like that when setting up audio, so I can try to experiment with a more advanced panel (perhaps have it optionally show instead of the simple panel to just play/stop the player) and share what that looks/feels like","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3944815589/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3944826194","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116623#issuecomment-3944826194","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116623","id":3944826194,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rIUVS","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T13:35:13Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T13:35:13Z","body":"I'm also wondering what happens when you click away from the stream in question. Will it keep playing? We'd be setting ourselves up for a situation where people click to play a sound file, not realizing it's long, and then wonder where the sound is coming from later because the element is no longer in focus.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3944826194/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3945129361","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116623#issuecomment-3945129361","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116623","id":3945129361,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rJeWR","user":{"login":"tvenclovas96","id":144885265,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKLGEQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/144885265?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96","html_url":"https://github.com/tvenclovas96","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T14:35:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T14:37:19Z","body":"> I'm also wondering what happens when you click away from the stream in question. Will it keep playing? We'd be setting ourselves up for a situation where people click to play a sound file, not realizing it's long, and then wonder where the sound is coming from later because the element is no longer in focus.\r\n\r\nIt keeps playing. If you switch scenes it will pause, and resume when you switch back. This is existing behaviour if you just enable the `playing` bool property. I don't think it's something to be concerned about since it already exists, and it's usually not a problem to keep track of audio stream players in your scene. (Would be cool to have an animated audio-stream icon for the node if it's playing, but that feels very out of scope)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3945129361/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3953867828","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116623#issuecomment-3953867828","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116623","id":3953867828,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rqzw0","user":{"login":"tvenclovas96","id":144885265,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKLGEQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/144885265?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96","html_url":"https://github.com/tvenclovas96","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvenclovas96/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type"